<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 72,345 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 72,345 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 72,345 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Tuesday compared to 63,780 tonnes in the same period on Monday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Tuesday     Jan 27</p>
<p>    Export cargo		11,255	 6,526</p>
<p>    Import cargo		61,090	57,254</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, three ships sailed and two berthed. In the next 24 hours, six are expected to sail and 13 are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Palm oil		 15,000	 Wawasan Courage   29/1</p>
<p>Palm oil		 15,000	 Wawasan Megah     29/1</p>
<p>Chemicals		10,550	 Bakri Orbitor     29/1</p>
<p>Containers		  600	 Contship Atlantic 29/1</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
